Fancy AI — Third-Party Acknowledgements
========================================

Fancy AI is built on the shoulders of excellent open-source projects and
services. Huge thanks to all of them. Each remains under its own license.

On-device inference
- llama.cpp — https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp (MIT)
  The local LLM engine (GGUF models, CPU/Hexagon NPU inference).
- whisper.cpp — https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp (MIT)
  On-device speech recognition.
- LiteRT-LM — https://github.com/google-ai-edge/LiteRT-LM (Apache License 2.0)
  On-device language-model runtime.
- sherpa-onnx — https://github.com/k2-fsa/sherpa-onnx (Apache License 2.0)
  On-device text-to-speech runtime.

Image generation
- MNN — https://github.com/alibaba/MNN (Apache License 2.0)
  CPU/OpenCL inference for Aura text encoding and image upscaling.
- Qualcomm AI Runtime (QAIRT/QNN) — Qualcomm Technologies, Inc.
  Redistributable runtime components used for supported NPU image generation; governed by
  the applicable Qualcomm SDK and redistribution terms.
- Local Dream — https://github.com/xororz/local-dream
  On-device Snapdragon NPU Stable Diffusion server.
- stable-diffusion.cpp (Hexagon NPU fork) — https://github.com/happyyzy/stable-diffusion.cpp (MIT)
  The DiT engine (FLUX.2, Z-Image, Qwen Image) with the ggml Hexagon backend;
  upstream https://github.com/leejet/stable-diffusion.cpp (MIT).
- Stable Diffusion WebUI Forge / AUTOMATIC1111 — local image-generation backends
  used over their SD Web API endpoints.

